# Files that belong in the repo but must not be served.
#
# outputDirectory is "." — the deployment serves the repo root — so anything
# left here becomes a public URL. These are excluded from the upload entirely,
# which is stronger than a redirect: the paths simply do not exist.
#
# templates/ and data/ are deliberately NOT listed. `node build.js` reads them
# during the build, so excluding them would break the deploy. They are served,
# which is untidy but harmless — neither is indexable prose.

# The working source for data/projects.json. Published as-is it would be a
# second, raw copy of every page under work/ — duplicate public content on a
# site that sells SEO.
case-studies/

# Build and authoring tooling: the image pipeline, the legal-page generator,
# and the Apps Script that receives the contact form.
tools/

# Markdown source for the legal pages. The pages themselves are committed HTML.
content/

# Design masters, already gitignored, listed for completeness.
Visual Assets/

.claude/

# Working notes and dead weight. README and the backups are not site content.
README.md
backup/
.agents/
skills-lock.json
